# Fixed defect 129, 2026-09-28, class (B), beside defect 126. Symptom: on a
# `str` match, an arm's `-` alone over `"a" => 10` had its join `certain`, and
# `check --apply` wrote `-"a" => 10`, which is `bad_operand`: a sign takes an
# integer or a character, never a string. Cause: the sign's join did not ask
# what it signs. It is a `guess` now, before the arm's `=>` and before a `|`
# (`selfhost/line_joins.hero`).
#
# A golden cannot hold a `guess`: this `.expected` is `--brief`, which prints
# no certainty, and a `.fixed` must check clean. So what this file pins is one
# diagnostic per break; the certainties are held by `selfhost/lexer.hero`'s
# defect 129 tests, which lex the same shapes.
#
# Corrected 2026-10-02, defect 159, lane h158: the deletion of the `-` is
# offered now, and `certain`, since no `-` signs a string (panel 185 R6), with
# no join beside it, and `check --apply` writes it: the `.fixed` beside this
# file is that program, which checks clean.

function pick(s: str) -> i64
    return match s
        "p" => 5
        #~v continuation_outside_brackets
        "a" => 10
        #~v continuation_outside_brackets
        "b" | "c" => 11
        _ => 20

function main()
    print(pick(s: "q"))
